{"Calling StringEscapeUtils.unescapeHtml4 on the OWASP sanitizer output reverts the sanitizer's entity-encoding of disallowed content, reintroducing raw </>  characters and potentially unsafe markup": 0.67527836561203, "normalizeValue unescapes HTML entities before sanitization, making it impossible to reason correctly about what the sanitizer actually blocked": 0.3818075656890869, "Duplicate-key detection startsWith(\"#\") check is applied to raw line, so comment lines with leading whitespace (e.g., \"  # comment\") will not be treated as comments and may be parsed as keys": 0.21430915594100952, "Blank lines containing whitespace are not considered empty because isEmpty() returns false, causing false duplicate-key detections or missed comments": 0.15796901285648346}